SCOPE OF THE ABOVE

The MIT licence above covers what was made for this repository:

  - the four patch files, the three tools, and the packaging
  - the showcase image and the mod icon
  - the documentation

No file of purpleyam's is included. Their Colorful Coats - Cats and Dogs! is
the origin of the idea, of the name, and of the colours: the seventeen tints
this mod uses are measurements of coats they painted, recovered by dividing
each coat by the sprite under it. The measuring is ours and the MIT covers
it; the choice of colours is theirs, and no licence is claimed over it. The
textures themselves are not reused - the mod they were painted for no longer
exists on its own, and they live in a different port:

  https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2388932599

If purpleyam would rather this mod did not carry their mod's name or their
colours, say so and it is renamed, repainted or taken down. Immediately, and
without discussion.

The animals are neither purpleyam's nor mine. They belong to Stray Dogs
(rescued) by Qux - itself the continuation of SpiderCamp's Dog Pack -, to
Let's Have a Cat! by akairo, to Vanilla Animals Expanded, and to RimWorld
itself. This mod ships no part of any of them and only patches them at load
time.

ATTRIBUTION.md records what was taken and what was made.
